heikh Lotfollah Mosque is a mosque on the eastern side of the Naqsh-e Jahan Square in Isfahan, built under Shah Abbas I in the early seventeenth century.</span></a></li><li class="enc-item has-img"><a href="/encyclopedia/sheikh-mujibur-rahman"><img class="enc-thumb" src="/images/encyclopedia/sheikh-mujibur-rahman.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="56" height="56"><span class="enc-name">Sheikh Mujibur Rahman</span><span class="enc-type">Person</span><span class="enc-snip">Sheikh Mujibur Rahman was the leader of the Awami League and the founding leader of Bangladesh.</span></a></li><li class="enc-item has-img"><a href="/encyclopedia/sheikh-ul-islam"><img class="enc-thumb" src="/images/encyclopedia/sheikh-ul-islam.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="56" height="56"><span class="enc-name">Sheikh ul-Islam</span><span class="enc-type">Institution</span><span class="enc-snip">Sheikh ul-Islam was the title of the chief religious authority in the Ottoman Empire, who headed the learned hierarchy of Islamic scholars.</span></a></li><li class="enc-item has-img"><a href="/encyclopedia/shelon-river"><img class="enc-thumb" src="/images/encyclopedia/shelon-river.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="56" height="56"><span class="enc-name">Shelon River</span><span class="enc-type">Place</span><span class="enc-snip">The Shelon is a river of north-western Russia, about 250 kilometres long, flowing north-east through the Pskov and Novgorod regions into Lake Ilmen.</span></a></li><li class="enc-item"><a href="/encyclopedia/shemamun"><span class="enc-name">Shemamun</span><span class="enc-type">Person</span><span class="enc-snip">Shemamun was a king of Makuria in Nubia in the late 13th century, repeatedly deposed and restored.</span></a></li><li class="enc-item"><a href="/encyclopedia/shen-baoxu"><span class="enc-name">Shen Baoxu</span><span class="enc-type">Person</span><span class="enc-snip">Shen Baoxu was a minister of the State of Chu who saved it after the invasion by Wu in 506 BCE.</span></